# Provider CLI and terminal sandbox

When running **Git hosting operations via the command line** (`gh`, `glab`, or shell scripts that wrap them), **do not use a sandboxed terminal**. Sandboxed execution **reliably fails** (auth, network, or CLI-specific errors).

**Do this instead:** run those commands with **full terminal permissions** (non-sandbox), or use **provider MCP adapters** / other non-CLI paths when the user prefers not to elevate terminal permissions.

Also applies to chained commands where **`gh`** or **`glab`** is an essential part of the same shell invocation.

Orchestration skills must resolve the provider first (**`.cursor/skills/provider/detect-provider/SKILL.md`**) and delegate to **`.cursor/skills/provider/github/SKILL.md`** or **`.cursor/skills/provider/gitlab/SKILL.md`** instead of embedding provider-specific CLI flags directly in command skills.
